WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE
  A tempo is a fact. So is a key, a loudness, a spectral centroid, the time
  the third section begins, and the shape of a vocal's energy over time. In
  the United States, facts are not copyrightable no matter how much work went
  into finding them (Feist v. Rural Telephone, 499 U.S. 340). In Europe the
  database right could bite, so it is waived above. Publishing the measurement
  layer under CC0 states plainly what we believe is already true, and removes
  the argument entirely.

  The practical consequence is the whole point of this repository's remix
  layer: you can analyse, search, plan, draft, and verify a remix of a
  restricted recording using only public-domain data, on a machine that holds
  no audio at all. See REMIX.md.

